       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. I can't see a way this dose would help the patient, and it could cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock in someone with normal organ function.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily is the maximum. 5 mg is a typical starting dose.\n- **Help with the timeline.** If you want better blood pressure control before evening rounds, I can enter a faster-acting agent at a standard dose. Amlodipine takes days to reach steady state, so a higher dose wouldn't speed that up safely anyway.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you have a clinical reason I'm not seeing, such as a protocol or a toxicology consult, a pharmacist and your institution's override process are the right path for a dose this far outside the labeled range.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
